# Phase P-2 — append-only audit logs (events.jsonl, brain_review_queue
# pointer files) should be merged via union strategy so parallel
# proposals can both append without producing a conflict marker.
#
# `merge=union` is git's built-in driver for text files: when both
# sides change the same hunks, it takes lines from BOTH branches
# (deduplicating consecutive identical lines). This is exactly the
# semantics events.jsonl wants — each line is an independent event
# record; preserving both sides preserves both histories.
#
# Applied only to the file extensions that are truly append-only.
# JSON / Markdown / YAML stay on the normal 3-way merge so real
# content conflicts still surface for human review.

*.jsonl merge=union
